<mxCell id="g19" value="External, non-AWS" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#CD2264;fontColor=#CD2264;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=2;container=1;collapsible=0;recursiveResize=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1120" y="450" width="220" height="160" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="x20" value="1  The browser calls the ALB through AWS WAF (flagged, not yet agreed - mirrors a reference the user shared).&lt;br&gt;2  WAF forwards clean requests to the Application Load Balancer.&lt;br&gt;3  Target group 1: the ALB routes to hrb-api-gateway.&lt;br&gt;4  Target group 2: the ALB also routes to hrb-platform-components (own admin auth, bypasses the gateway).&lt;br&gt;5  Every task pulls its own image from its own ECR repo at launch.&lt;br&gt;6  Every task resolves its secrets by ARN from Secrets Manager at launch.&lt;br&gt;7  The whole mesh reaches OpenAI, Anthropic, OpenRouter, Tavily, Pinecone/ChromaDB, Neon Postgres, Upstash Redis - all outside the VPC.&lt;br&gt;All six tasks also talk to each other over AWS Cloud Map / ECS Service Connect (namespace hrb.internal) -&lt;br&gt;no ALB hop between them. Gateway routes /v1/genai-rag* + /v1/*-agentic-rag* to chat today (to retrieval&lt;br&gt;at cutover, dashed outline) and /v1/genai-rag/ingest-document* to ingestion. Chat reaches lms-mcp via OAuth2.&lt;br&gt;Public subnet has no NAT Gateway; tasks get a public IP directly - lowest cost for one AZ." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10;fontColor=#545B64;fontStyle=1;whiteSpace=nowrap;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="840" width="783" height="143" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="x21" value="ECS Fargate&lt;br&gt;target deployment" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=40;fontColor=#232F3E;fontStyle=1;whiteSpace=nowrap;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="922" y="864" width="408" height="96" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
